{#
    The rail, top to bottom as the prototype draws it: the brand, the household
    you are in, where you can go, a way to add a subscription, and who you are.

    Fixed at 240px on anything wide enough for it and replaced by the tab bar
    in `tabbar.twig` below 768px. Both draw the same lists, so the narrow
    screen loses the layout and none of the reach.

    `nav`    the Navigation for this page
    `shell`  the ShellContext (the household label and the badge), or null

    At its foot, the release this instance runs (`version.twig`).

    What is not here: the design's Upgrade Plan card. Renovo is self-hosted and
    there is no plan to upgrade to.
#}
<aside class="sidebar">
    {#
        The mark sits in a tile on the dark rails — white, so the gradient
        reads — and bare on the light ones. The tile's colour and padding are
        palette tokens (`--logo-tile`, `--logo-pad`), so which rail gets one is
        decided by the palette rather than by this template.
    #}
    <a class="sidebar-brand" href="/">
        <span class="logo-tile">
            <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 460 427" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <use href="#renovo-mark"></use>
            </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="sidebar-brand-text">
            <span class="sidebar-brand-name">{{ instance_name }}</span>
            <span class="sidebar-tagline">{{ t('shell.tagline') }}</span>
        </span>
    </a>

    {% if shell and shell.household %}
        {% include 'partials/household_label.twig' with {'household': shell.household} only %}
    {% endif %}

    <div class="sidebar-nav">
        <nav aria-label="{{ t('nav.primary') }}">
            {% include 'partials/nav_links.twig' with {
                'links': nav.primary,
                'badges': shell and shell.subscriptionCount is not null
                    ? {'subscriptions': shell.subscriptionCount}
                    : {}
            } only %}
        </nav>

        {% if nav.tools is not empty %}
            <nav aria-labelledby="rail-tools-heading">
                <p class="sidebar-group-heading" id="rail-tools-heading">{{ t('nav.household_tools') }}</p>
                {% include 'partials/nav_links.twig' with {'links': nav.tools} only %}
            </nav>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-foot">
        {#
            Accent-filled: adding a subscription is the application's main
            action, and the rail is where it is found on every screen. The
            accent carries its own ink (`--accent-ink`) in every palette, so it
            reads on a dark rail and a light one alike. It is a link to the real
            form before it is a dialog.
        #}
        {% if can(scope, 'subscription.create') %}
            <a class="sidebar-add" href="/subscriptions/new" data-opens-dialog="quick-add">
                {{ icon('add-circle', 'nav-icon') }}
                <span>{{ t('subscriptions.add_subscription') }}</span>
            </a>
        {% endif %}

        {% include 'partials/user_card.twig' with {'account': nav.account, 'user': current_user} only %}

        {% include 'partials/version.twig' %}
    </div>
</aside>
